/* The main menu in the original look, over the pause menu's (../pause_menu/style.rcss): the title screen with the
   original's start menu box (main_menu.c: renderInitialMenu; capture title_menu).

   The title image (TITLE2, 320 x 240) keeps its 4:3 proportions in the middle of a wide screen, on black. The box is
   at (72, 50), 176 pixels wide; its rows start at x 82 and are 12 pixels apart, and the selector is a 152-pixel
   outline from x 78. The original fills the box with a gradient from four corners (#000070, #000050, #000030,
   #000010); a gradient from top to bottom of the corners' averages (#000060 to #000020) stands in for it, since a
   four-corner gradient needs shaders the UI does not have. The box is as tall as its entries: this menu has five and
   the prompt, the original four. Its own title stays hidden: the title image carries the game's name. It is wider
   than the original's, 640dp, so that the longest label (Spanish's "Texto con aspecto original") and its value keep
   a gap: the original's options had no values. */

#scrim {
	background-color: #000000;
	decorator: image(title-screen contain center center);
}

#panel {
	position: absolute;
	left: 50%;
	top: 150dp;
	width: 640dp;
	margin-left: -320dp;
	padding: 12dp 0 12dp 18dp;
	border: 3dp #90d9fa;
	border-right-color: #4a9fc5;
	background-color: transparent;
	decorator: image(box-tl scale-none left top) border-box, image(box-tr scale-none right top) border-box,
		image(box-bl scale-none left bottom) border-box, image(box-br scale-none right bottom) border-box,
		vertical-gradient(#000060 #000020);
}

#title {
	display: none;
}

#panel button {
	width: 568dp;
}

#prompts {
	margin-right: 18dp;
}
